# gather — withheld from a body with no hands (see AnatomyCapability, Verb.RequiredCapabilities)
#
# The same object, thought about by two bodies. --fill-party gives the party a beast (the hyena
# Brindletail at seed 42), played by a click on its token — every gate reads the member played.
#
# GATHER is a Handcraft verb. The protagonist is offered it on the bush; the hyena, with the same
# bush in front of it, is not — the goal is not in its list at all, so `goal gather` falls back and
# stdout carries
#   [debug] --goal-only 'gather': no such goal here — drawing from all N.
# The act that then runs is the proof: `goal` falls back to the other goals when its verb is not
# offered, so whatever the hyena does, it is not gathering.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --fill-party --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Field" --period noon --observe-only "Test Berry Bush"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180
expect [KENRYC GREYGATE]

# --- the human: gather is offered, and the act says so --------------------------
strategy succeed
goal gather
click observe "Test Berry Bush"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think "Test Berry Bush"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
expect-state trees "verb=gather"

# --- the beast, on the same object ----------------------------------------------
click member Brindletail
wait
expect [BRINDLETAIL]

# No gather in its goals, but it still acts: the gate narrowed the goal list rather than emptying it.
goal gather
click observe "Test Berry Bush"
choose birdsong
advance 12 180
click think "Test Berry Bush"
choose birdsong
advance 12 180
click act 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-no-verb gather
expect [BRINDLETAIL]

# This script tests an ABSENCE: the hyena must NOT be offered gather. `--goal-only gather` finding
# no such goal is therefore the assertion passing, so its miss must not fail the run.
allow-flag-miss --goal-only
quit
